WEBVTT

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.990
August 11th

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.740
Yuuki, wake up!

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.190
Yuuki!

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.260
Wha...

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.160
What is it?

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.480
I'm still sleepy.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.380
Hanada-senpai's game has already started!

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.720
Good morning!

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.680
Why didn't the alarm go off?

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.760
I turned it off, so that we

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.230
could all sleep in the day after the match.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.940
But you're the one who said we should 
get up early and watch her game!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.340
I forget other stuff when 
I get absorbed in one thing!

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.340
Saki-san!

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.620
Just a little longer...

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.620
And the opening dealer is 
Shindouji's Hanada Kirame!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.620
So Miyanaga will be the last dealer?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.160
That might be a dangerous constellation.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.670
Captain!

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.220
Morning.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:11.340
Good morning!

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.000
Heya!

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.300
Good morning.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.510
You should have woken us.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.760
But you guys were sleeping so soundly.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.270
Our senpai from middle 
school is playing in this match.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.910
Oh, sorry.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.590
You mean the person from 
Takatoobara Middle School?

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.110
This Hanada Kirame-san?

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.790
Shindouji - 2nd Year

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.940
I was surprised when she suddenly appeared

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.220
when I was watching the second round matches.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.460
That's heartless of you, Nodo-chan.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.160
You didn't know about it, either.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.160
Shiraitodai - 3rd Year

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.160
<i>That's Saki-san's older sister.</i>

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:50.870
The inter-high champion really 
is strong, as you'd expect.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.300
Yeah.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.240
But the girl from Achiga is 
doing a good job keeping her

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.490
in check by holding on to all those dora.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.120
But it looks like that's making 
Achiga's hand a little cramped.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:06.670
<i>Achiga... holds on to the dora.</i>

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.190
Achiga - 2nd Year

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.520
That's Kuro-san!

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.070
Do you know her?

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.450
Achiga is the school I went to 
back when I lived in Nara.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.260
Huh? You went to Achiga Girls'?

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.950
Nodoka, you never noticed her before?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.070
I guess I never really focused when 
I looked at the match board.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.710
You never change.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.280
Here. This is Achiga Girls'.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.670
<b>Achiga Girls' Academy 
Coach: Akado Harue 

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.790
Is it all right if I run over to the auditorium?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.670
Be careful.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.320
I will!

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.430
I'm coming, too!

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.190
I'll bring some tacos to Senpai!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.940
Morning...

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.560
What's going on?

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.870
We thought we'd go over to the auditorium.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.820
Come with us, Saki-chan!

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:03.230
Huh? You mean now?

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.990
Shiraitodai (West Tokyo)
 Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
 Achiga Girls' (Nara)
 Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.930
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:40.770
<b>Hand 13: 
Old Friends</b>

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.380
Almost there!

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.830
<i>Right now, my sister's in there.</i>

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.010
Saki...

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.450
Saki-san?

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.700
Um... I...

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.050
Why don't you two go on ahead?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.700
I'll be along a little later.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.210
There's a restroom inside, 
if that's what you need.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.210
All right.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.330
Do you have the captain's cell phone?

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.110
Yeah.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.520
Then we'll go on ahead.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.480
Okay.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.520
Yuuki, let's go.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.970
Yeah!

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.590
Darn it! We can't get inside!

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.660
I guess when you get to the semifinals,

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.410
it's packed even in the morning.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.540
It looks like the first 
players' match is over, too.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.620
Maybe we should've just 
stayed at the inn to watch.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.640
Nodo-chan, the only fly in your 
pie is that you lose your cool

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.060
when you get excited.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:04.250
Yuuki, the saying is "fly in the ointment."

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.470
I wasn't expecting that response.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.840
Besides, I'm full of flaws, 
so that idiom doesn't fit.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.550
Your only flaw is being five 
kilos heavier than a girl

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:18.190
who's the same height as you, 
even though you're skinnier.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.490
Hey! Is that you, Haramura-san?

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:21.520
Huh?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.630
The lady from the magazine...

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.900
Is the hall completely full?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.070
Yeah...

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.120
Come to the press room.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.120
We've got a drink dispenser, too.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.470
Oh, but...

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.280
Wouldn't we be in the way?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.930
For me, it'd be perfect!

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.580
Just let me take your picture afterwards.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.550
A picture of Nodo-chan?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.480
<b>Wow!</b>

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.590
You mean a s-s-sexy picture?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.670
Out of the question.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.050
There was a girl who collapsed at 
the end of the first players' match.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.580
I was told to follow her and talk to her,

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:56.100
but I'd greatly prefer you
over some indiscreet scoop.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.010
An article about Nodo-chan would 
end up indecent in another way.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.750
I don't deny that.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:07.400
Anyway, the girl who passed out 
wasn't Hanada-senpai, was it?

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.970
I've never even seen her anemic.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.200
<b>Marvelous!</b>

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.200
Marvelous!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.000
I guess that's true!

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:26.880
Nodoka...

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.060
Shizuno!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.350
Ako!

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:37.750
Kuro-san!

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.230
It's been so long...

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.200
Do you know these girls?

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.030
Yes.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.990
They're friends from when I lived in Nara.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:50.440
Friends?!

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.130
<i>Oh yeah, I remember.</i>

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.750
I was just thinking that 
you remind me a tiny bit

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.830
of two friends I had back in grade school.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:05.390
<i>So that means... they are 
Nodo-chan's old friends.</i>

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.550
Nodoka, we're definitely 
going to be in the finals.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.630
So you have to be there, too!

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:13.010
In the finals!

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:17.350
I can't make any promises,

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.230
but I'm personally going to 
do everything that I can.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.730
Then we'll see you at the finals!

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:30.370
Yes.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.630
Sit back and relax.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.090
That's so good!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.980
Thank you so much.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.400
Seconds, please!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.730
You didn't have to get us these lunches, too.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.260
Sure.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.340
It's not a problem!

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.600
After all, I'll be getting 
something much better from you.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.650
Here's your second helping.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:06.480
Yay! Thanks!

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:08.850
I feel terribly rude asking after 
you gave us this food, but...

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.510
I wonder if it's over.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.990
Oh, that's me.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:19.960
<b>No</b>

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.050
"No"?

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:22.490
Hello?

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:24.830
Nodoka-chan...

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:26.820
Where are you right now?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.590
Want to come over here and eat with us?

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.760
I'm still outside...

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.890
I think... I'm going to go back to the inn.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.250
I see...

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:54.190
I should probably go back with you,

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.050
Delicious!

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.410
but it looks like I have to repay 
them for four lunch boxes...

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.160
Yes.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:04.170
I'll eat back at the inn, where 
they have the breakfast buffet.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.660
Oh, that's only until nine?

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.680
Well, I'll figure out something.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:10.890
Uh-huh.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.280
Talk to you later.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.660
Guess I'll go...

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:55.480
<i>See?</i>

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.760
<i>You can see so much better 
if you lie on your stomach.</i>

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.000
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.040
<i>I can see the sparkling just fine standing.</i>

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.400
<i>Do you like fish that much?</i>

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.450
<i>They're fun to watch and they taste good!</i>

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:09.770
<i>You enjoy them both ways?!</i>

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.760
<i>It's my dream to open an aquarium.</i>

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.800
<i>Not to be a sushi chef?</i>

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:20.860
<i>I used to like to swim, but I 
don't think I could do it now.</i>

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:24.350
<i>So the fish do all the swimming for me.</i>

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.680
<i>When I build my aquarium,</i>

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.870
<i>you and your sister should come visit.</i>

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:31.910
<i>Sure.</i>

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:37.870
Saki!

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:42.120
Saki!

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.640
We came to visit!

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:47.830
Koromo-chan?

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.220
Not "chan"!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.230
Nonoka isn't here?

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.360
She's at the auditorium to watch 
her old friends play in their match.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.820
Oh?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.280
She has friends in the other block?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.490
That's pretty cool.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:07.150
<i>I wonder what Nodoka-chan's up to.</i>

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:14.860
I was going to wait until the game was over,

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:15.830
but I can't wait any longer.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.460
Can we start now, Haramura-san?

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:20.390
What, exactly?

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:21.720
The sexy article.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:27.070
I was wondering if you could tell us 
about your connection to Achiga Girls'.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.470
Okay... sure.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.880
Nodo-chan, you're holding out on us!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:44.110
No, it's just that it looks like 
your voice recorder is turned off,

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.950
so I thought you were still getting ready...

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:49.700
You're right! Huh?!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.040
Umm, is it this?

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.200
There've been about five times 
when Nishida-san asked me

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.770
to transcribe an interview, and 
the data she gave me was blank.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.370
Kumiko-chan, you just 
started working here, too!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.260
I'm screwing up a lot...

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.300
There.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.110
Recording has started!

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.710
Please go ahead and start.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:07.650
Right.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:12.810
Achiga Girls' Academy was the 
school I attended when I lived in Nara.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.340
That's it?

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:17.310
I guess so.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.760
I think I have some pictures 
from that time on the blog.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.920
You have a blog?

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.940
Send the URL to the address on my card!

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:26.530
Okay.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.730
This is how to get it on the big screen.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.750
It's not my blog...

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:33.750
It's not?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.740
There it is!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.460
A River Swim

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.460
Harue Journal

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:38.460
"A river... swim"?

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.260
It's dated four years ago, in summer.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.680
That was the last summer of grade school.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.050
If you go a little below that entry, 
there should be a picture of all of us.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.430
Let's see.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:55.130
The girl to the right is you, Nodoka-chan?

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.140
Yes.

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:59.790
There's one place that doesn't look 
like it belongs on a grade schooler.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.020
You're right.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.320
A child's school bag on that body...

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.550
It's a crime.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.780
We're still recording, aren't we?

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:10.690
The foremost one on the left 
is Matsumi Kuro-san, right?

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:12.500
Achiga's first player this year.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:17.180
The girl beside you is Achiga's fifth player... um...

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.380
Takakamo Shizuno.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.210
Right.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:23.380
And then, all the way to the left is...

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.860
Kataoka-san?

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.840
It's a girl who looks like me!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.660
That's not Yuuki, that's Ako.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.800
Atarashi Ako.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.020
You mean Achiga Girls' third player?!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:35.640
That Atarashi Ako-chan?

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.840
Impossible!

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.240
That can't be true!

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.900
Why are you looking at me?

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:47.620
So, you were already acquainted with 
three of Achiga Girls' regular players?

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:48.650
That's right.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.090
I spent my sixth and seventh 
grade years in Nara.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:58.540
Most of the time I spent with them 
was in sixth grade, though.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:04.090
Players in regional tournaments 
often have some connection,

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:07.550
but it's not so common on the national level.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.590
Unless you're lucky with the match-ups,

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.590
<b>Kiyosumi</b>

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.430
you're not very likely to run into each other.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.430
<b>Achiga Girls'</b>

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:12.960
This competition has

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:15.310
Kiyosumi and Achiga playing in 
completely opposite brackets.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.630
It would be nice if you could meet in the finals.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:22.180
Yes.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.250
The fifth players' match will soon begin.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.900
Will all participating players...

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.200
This way!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.460
Please let us pass!

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:34.530
H-Hold on, there!

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.210
What do you think you're doing?

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.420
Entry is prohibited beyond this point.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.200
Only players may enter.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.210
What?

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.910
But I am a player!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.400
Only players participating 
in today's competition.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.670
We can't let anything happen.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.590
How are we going to get this inside?

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:54.590
Huh?

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.180
Hanada-senpai!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:58.390
Huh?

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.270
Oh, it's been forever!

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.770
It's over!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:07.420
That's it for the first game of the semifinals!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.150
<b>Shindouji Girls'</b>

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:27.610
Um, would you like to have some of this?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.010
Big Hall ->

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.010
Himematsu
High School 
Mahjong Club

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.050
What?

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.950
Let's meet at

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.230
That was fast.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.940
What's this supposed to mean, Hayari-san?

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:55.450
Oh, my. You're the first one here, Yoshiko-chan!

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:07.500
The ramen noodle of Japan is truly delicious.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.250
You even eat that when we're 
outside? Unbelievable.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.050
But of course!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:18.340
My time here is limited, but 
the Japanese ramen is infinite!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:22.110
It's also the perfect meal to eat before a match.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:27.400
Where are the others?

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.860
They went ahead to the 
auditorium with the coach.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.200
I see.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.010
Sensei!

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.040
Good luck, master!

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:39.780
Yup!

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.900
Good luck to you too, Mega-chan!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.240
Fight, miss!

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.580
Leave it to me.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:52.170
Are you fine going like that?

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.770
Oh, yeah.

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:04.080
Well, shall we?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:04.720
Yay!

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.730
You're all here...

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:09.350
Then it's off to the semifinals!

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.910
Here. Good luck.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:15.990
Thank you.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:23.490
I'm back.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.780
Good work, Arata.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:26.830
Welcome back.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:31.220
The game is starting soon. 
Want me to take your place?

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.120
Nodoka's semifinal game, huh?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.920
What are you going to do, Shizu?

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.190
You can go and watch, Shizu-chan.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.640
No, I'll keep playing.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.100
You're not curious?

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.310
We made a promise...

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.350
to meet at the finals!

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.360
Only two days remain in the
inter-high team tournament.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.990
Today is the second game of the semifinals.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.520
It's a fight for the two remaining spots.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:00.470
Commentator/Announcer
 Murayoshi Misaki

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.320
Pro Player Noyori,

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.390
what should we be paying attention to today?

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:04.850
Professional Analyst
 Noyori Risa

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.040
Pro Player Noyori?

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:07.950
Everything.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:12.160
I wasn't asking for a polite or 
unoffensive answer like that,

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.210
but a particular point to focus on.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.020
U-U—

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.150
Uniforms...

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.300
All right. Thank you.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.120
Is that pair really doing the commentary?

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.510
Noyori-san isn't very articulate at all.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:30.590
Apparently, when she looks angry, 
that just means she's excited.

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:31.520
Not that I'd know.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:35.530
And this announcer's tone is too harsh, I feel.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.690
Yeah...

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.910
Still, they do seem to get along pretty well.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:44.070
We will now introduce 
the participating schools.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.160
Here we go.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.790
First off, we've got Himematsu High 
School, representing South Osaka.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:54.290
These veterans from Kansai are 
practically regulars at the semifinals.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.640
Zenno, their former coach 
who collapsed last year

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:01.140
at the spring tournament, has 
come to cheer them on as well.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:02.550
<i>Coach...</i>

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.760
Next, we have Kiyosumi High 
School, representing Nagano.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.100
This newcomer school has

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.430
the inter-middle champion,
Haramura Nodoka, in their ranks.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.080
They made it to the nationals by 
defeating Ryuumonbuchi High School,

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.350
who were on a rampage last year.

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:17.260
They've made it to the semifinals,

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.970
and amazingly, they took first place in 
both the first and second round matches!

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.470
Why are they only showing Haramura?!

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:23.610
Nonoka!

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:26.570
Are they going to be the dark 
horse of this second game?

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.330
And next, we have the second seed.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:31.680
Rinkai Girls', representing East Tokyo.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:33.880
Until last year, they were 
a very cosmopolitan team

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.390
comprised of only exchange students,

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:38.460
but this year, they're down 
to four exchange students.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:40.850
They're still cosmopolitan!

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:42.070
You're right.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.760
And another newcomer!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:48.010
Usuzan High School, 
representing South Hokkaido!

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.930
Then I'm off.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.270
What? You're taking that cape again?

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.350
It would be a waste not to!

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:56.980
I'm counting on you.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.610
I've got this!

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:06.070
And it's finally time!

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:09.740
Each school is sending their 
first player to the stage!

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.000
The first players' match of the 
second game of the semifinals

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:22.450
is about to begin!

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:28.500
<i>In the 21st century,</i>

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.880
<i>the number of mahjong players around
the world is in the hundreds of millions,</i>

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:37.110
<i>and the professional players 
have an avid following.</i>

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.940
<i>Even at the high school level, 
a large-scale national tournament</i>

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.400
<i>is held every year.</i>

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:46.670
<i>That's where the high 
school players compete</i>

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:50.440
<i>in order to make it into the 
league of professionals.</i>

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:56.020
<i>This is the path of the girls 
who were aiming for the top.</i>

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:48.280
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:45.710
Saki...
